---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.js';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="How this website uses cookies, local storage and third-party requests, including Google Fonts, and how you can control them."
  lede="This policy explains the cookies and similar technologies used on flourmillingpro.com. The short version: no advertising cookies, no analytics cookies, no data selling."
>
  <h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. They can remember
    preferences, keep a session open, measure traffic or support advertising. Similar technologies
    include local storage, pixels and third-party requests that load resources such as fonts.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What this site uses</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Category</th><th>Used?</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Strictly necessary</td><td>Yes, where required by hosting</td><td>Serve pages, apply security controls and route requests through the CDN.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Preferences</td><td>No</td><td>We do not set a cookie to remember language or display settings.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Analytics</td><td>No</td><td>We do not run Google Analytics or another traffic-measurement cookie.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Advertising / retargeting</td><td>No</td><td>No advertising networks, pixels or retargeting tags.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>3. Hosting and security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served through Cloudflare. Cloudflare may process technical request data — IP
    address, requested URL, user agent, timestamp and security signals — to deliver the site and
    protect it from abuse. Its own privacy terms apply to that processing. We do not use Cloudflare
    analytics or advertising products on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Google Fonts</h2>
  <p>
    Pages load the typefaces Inter and Barlow Condensed from Google Fonts. When your browser
    requests those files, Google receives your IP address, browser information and the page that
    requested the font. This is a third-party request, not a cookie set by us. Google's privacy
    policy applies: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you prefer to avoid this request, you can block third-party fonts in your browser or use a
    content blocker. The site remains readable with system fonts.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Consent</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not currently set analytics, advertising or preference cookies, no consent banner
    is displayed. If we introduce a non-essential cookie or tracking technology, we will update this
    policy and, where required, ask for consent before it is set.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your browser controls</h2>
  <p>
    You can block, delete or restrict cookies in your browser settings. The controls differ by
    browser; look for “Privacy”, “Cookies and site data” or “Content settings”. Blocking all cookies
    may affect some websites, but should not prevent you from reading this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also use private browsing, a content blocker or a DNS-level filter. We do not respond to
    “Do Not Track” signals differently because we do not run cross-site tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We review this policy when the site, hosting or third-party services change. The revised version
    will be posted here with a new date. Material changes will be communicated where required by
    law.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about cookies or privacy: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    See also our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
